Rime initially felt to me like a  mishmash of journey the Last Guardian  the witness and brothers a tale of two  suns which is handy because I like all  those games thankfully from what I  gathered in our recent hour-long creevy  though rhyme doesn't have the  aggravating controls of the Last  Guardian probably because your furry  companion is capsized and not elephant  sized and it doesn't feature the  occasional frustrating difficulty spikes  of the witness perhaps even more  importantly so far it doesn't feel like  it's borrowing too heavily from any of  these games to check out our latest  gameplay clips and trailers for I'm do  hit that subscribe button but for now  let me give you a better idea of the  game during our preview all I could  think was how much my recent gaming  habits could do with a palette refresh  alike rhyme after spending 60 hours with  horizon zero dawn and another hundred  plus hours with persona 5 I'm so ready  for a game that isn't afraid to be quiet  to just let you move slowly at your own  pace take your time with puzzles or  listen to waves crashing up against  ancient buildings that isn't to say  there's nothing tense about rhyme if you  caught our recent gameplay clip you'll  see a section where the boys evading the  claws of a giant bird but there is still  plenty of time for scenery admiring  pillar climbing and Fox / friending  there's no dialogue in rhyme so much  like in journey or brothers a tale of  two sons you'll need to pay attention to  try and interpret what's happening on  your own rime uses painted murals placed  throughout the world to hint at who the  protagonist is where he came from and  what's going on in the world you may  have noticed from the gameplay you've  been watching over the last minute or  two that there really aren't a lot of  characters in the game apart from the  protagonist which evokes a mysterious  and lonely vibe it's a feeling that is  exacerbated by the fact that every so  often a mysterious figure pops up and  subsequently disappears every time you  get close to them rime is essentially  linear with some large explorable  sections that open up through puzzle  solving but I don't mind that I think  linear games get a bad rap but I  appreciate how you're able to get a very  specific vision communicated from  developer to player as a result of being  funneled down a particular  the paths rhyme producer Cody Bradley  told us the team put a lot of work into  tweaking the difficulty curve to ensure  players would feel challenged but not  overwhelmed while it aired on the side  of ease since we were early in the game  that generally seems to ring true at  least in our short preview session  sequencers tended to follow the same  pattern the player is introduced to a  new mechanic with a basic puzzle and the  following uses of that mechanic  gradually ramp up in difficulty beyond  the puzzling though the world is really  inviting the ico ask art style fits  really nicely with the feel of the game  which is a little bit mysterious and a  little bit magical what really brought  it a step up for me with the little  details when jumping upon a suspended  metal platform the structure clangs and  bends under your weight you get a trophy  for not crushing any bird eggs on your  way up an ancient building and you can  choose to either bait a wild pig with a  tasty treat or scare it to the area you  need it to be much like The Last  Guardian it also puts care into giving  you the feeling that you aren't  embodying just any protagonist but a  child from the way the boy runs from  place to place to his infectious join  climbing high objects or solving puzzles  by chucking a ball across a room the age  of your protagonist really shines  through as you progress if the Fox is  around the boy will say hello to it and  if he's on his own he'll hum to himself  it's too early to make a call in the  entire game but personally I think if  developers care enough to get the little  things right it's a sign that the  overall game direction has been treated  with care too  [Music]
 

